Subject: libmisc/walk_tree.c: define IFTODT() when the libc lacks it

Why: bionic's <dirent.h> defines the DT_* constants but not the IFTODT() conversion macro that
glibc and musl provide, so getfacl/setfacl -R fail to compile ("call to undeclared function").
The fallback is the same definition glibc uses ((mode & S_IFMT) >> 12).
Source: written for this module
(see ndk/REFERENCES.md for the sources checked); same definition as glibc and musl <dirent.h>.

--- a/libmisc/walk_tree.c
+++ b/libmisc/walk_tree.c
@@ -32,6 +32,11 @@
 
 #include "walk_tree.h"
 
+#ifndef IFTODT
+/* bionic <dirent.h> has DT_* but not the glibc/BSD IFTODT() macro */
+#define IFTODT(mode) (((mode) & 0170000) >> 12)
+#endif
+
 struct dir_stack_entry {
 	struct dir_stack_entry *parent;
 	DIR *stream;
